 Analysis</source><year>1994</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>1079</fpage><lpage>1080</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7846315</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1539-6924.1994.tb00078.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zheng</surname><given-names>Q</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>On the exact hazard and survival functions of the MVK stochastic carcinogenesis model</article-title><source>Risk Analysis</source><year>1994</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>1081</fpage><lpage>1084</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7846316</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1539-6924.1994.tb00079.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Moolgavkar</surname><given-names>SH</given-names></name><name><surname>Luebeck</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Two-event model for carcinogenesis: Biological, mathematical, and statistical considerations</article-title><source>Risk Analysis</source><year>1990</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>323</fpage><lpage>341</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2195604</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1539-6924.1990.tb01053.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hoogenveen</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Harvey</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Andersen</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Slob</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>An alternative exact solution of the two-stage clonal growth model of cancer</article-title><source>Risk Analysis</source><year>1999</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>9</fpage><lpage>14</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-g